BEGIN

1. Define the graph with edge costs.
2. Define the heuristic value h(n) for each node.
3. Initialize the priority queue with the start node P.
4. Set the cost of P to 0.
5. WHILE the priority queue is not empty:
      a. Remove the node with the lowest f(n).
      b. If the node is S:
             Reconstruct and display the path.
             STOP.
      c. For each neighbor of the current node:
             Calculate the new path cost g(n).
             Calculate f(n) = g(n) + h(n).
             If the new path is cheaper:
                  Update its cost and parent.
                  Add it to the priority queue.
6. If the goal is not reached:
      Display "Path not found".

END
